gm-method (server-fs vs client-URL relative-import symmetry for shared helper modules consumed from TWO different resolution contexts): a module imported by BOTH a server-side Node `import()` (resolved against the importing file's real filesystem path) AND a client-side blob-URL-rewritten sandboxed-app import (resolved against a SERVED URL prefix that may not mirror the filesystem layout 1:1, e.g. an app-loader that mounts one directory tree at `/apps/` and a sibling directory tree at root `/`) needs the shared helper to live somewhere BOTH resolution schemes reach with the SAME relative path -- typically a subdirectory already inside the asymmetric-mount tree (e.g. `apps/_lib/`), not a directory that is siblings-on-disk but asymmetric-under-the-static-mounts. Diagnosed by: reading the actual static-mount table (prefix->dir pairs) rather than assuming disk-sibling directories resolve the same way once served, then confirming BOTH the server boot log (an AppLoader syntax/resolve error names the exact missing path) and a live browser network-tab load (200 vs 404) before trusting either resolution guess.